// Unlike find_familiar.ron (a real agent-driven, permanent companion), this
// servant performs no in-engine task/chore mechanic -- no such system
// exists, and this spell has no combat fit either way. It maps cleanly onto
// the recipe already used by the shipped illusion phantasms
// (illusion/silent_image.ron and siblings): `alignment: Some(Passive)` (no
// will of its own), `with_agent: false` (no independent behaviour to run),
// `incorporeal: true` (approximates "unseen"/non-solid), `has_health: false`
// + `phantom_illusion: true` (vanishes the moment anything actually hits
// it -- a reasonable stand-in for D&D's "1 HP, destroyed by any attack"),
// `delete_after_expiry: true` for the client-side pre-expiry flicker. The
// only real change from that recipe is `duration`: a full hour instead of
// the illusions' 60-180s, matching this spell's much longer nominal
// lifetime. `body: Object(Pebble)` reuses minor_illusion_image.ron's own
// "small, unobtrusive placeholder" body rather than inventing a new asset.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.75,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: Object(Pebble),
        scale: None,
        has_health: false,
        use_npc_name: false,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        duration: Some((
            secs: 3600,
            nanos: 0,
        )),
        alignment: Some(Passive),
        with_agent: false,
        incorporeal: true,
        phantom_illusion: true,
        delete_after_expiry: true,
    ),
)
